## Why This Is Asked
This question probes practical security design for shared edge environments with tenant isolation, policy distribution, and runtime attestation.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation and WASM sandboxing
- Hardware-backed attestation (TPM/SGX)
- SBOM verification and delta policy updates
- Key management in HSMs and rotation strategies
- Revocation and rollback workflows

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: verifyPolicy and attestation check
async function loadPolicy(node, policyPackage) {
  const {sig, hash} = policyPackage;
  if (!verifySig(hash, sig, node.publicKey)) throw new Error('Invalid policy');
  if (!await attestationCheck(node)) throw new Error('Untrusted node');
  // apply policy
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test revocation paths for long-lived sessions?
- What are the trade-offs between delta updates and full policy refresh in terms of latency and risk?

## Why This Is Asked

Evaluates expertise in designing secure update systems for distributed edge infrastructure with unreliable connectivity, requiring comprehensive threat modeling around supply chain security, key management, and operational resilience.

## Key Concepts

- Device attestation and secure boot verification
- The Update Framework (TUF) and cryptographically signed deltas
- Atomic upgrade mechanisms with rollback protection
- Key rotation, revocation, and compromise containment strategies
- Bandwidth-efficient delivery and cryptographic implementations

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: verify signature and apply delta
function verifyAndApply(payload, signature, publicKey) {
  if (!ed25519.verify(signature, payload, publicKey)) {
    throw new Error('Invalid signature');
  }
  const decryptedPayload = aesGcm.decrypt(payload, encryptionKey);
  return applyDelta(decryptedPayload);
}
```

